================================================================================
1. The Open Screen Library (openscreen)
================================================================================

Upstream:   https://chromium.googlesource.com/openscreen/
License:    BSD 3-Clause ("Copyright The Chromium Authors")

CastMirror's protocol core (`core/`) is an independent Kotlin re-implementation
of the Cast Streaming sender, written by studying the openscreen reference
implementation. The following files are ports or close derivatives of specific
openscreen source files (the corresponding upstream file is named in each
Kotlin file's header comment) and are therefore derivative works of openscreen:

  core/cast/streaming/crypto/FrameCrypto.kt
      <- cast/streaming/impl/frame_crypto.cc
  core/cast/streaming/rtp/RtpPacketizer.kt
      <- cast/streaming/impl/rtp_packetizer.cc
  core/cast/streaming/rtp/RtpDefines.kt
      <- cast/streaming/impl/rtp_defines.h
  core/cast/streaming/rtcp/SenderReportBuilder.kt
      <- cast/streaming/impl/sender_report_builder.cc
  core/cast/streaming/rtcp/CompoundRtcpParser.kt
      <- cast/streaming/impl/compound_rtcp_parser.cc
  core/cast/streaming/rtcp/RtcpDefines.kt
      <- cast/streaming/impl/rtcp_common.{h,cc}
  core/cast/streaming/rtcp/NtpTime.kt
      <- cast/streaming/impl/ntp_time.{h,cc}
  core/cast/streaming/rtcp/FrameIdExpansion.kt
      <- cast/streaming/impl/expanded_value_base.h
  core/cast/streaming/Sender.kt
      <- cast/streaming/impl/sender_impl.{h,cc}
  core/cast/streaming/SenderPacketRouter.kt
      <- cast/streaming/impl/sender_packet_router.{h,cc}
  core/cast/streaming/UdpTransport.kt
      <- platform/impl/udp_socket_posix.cc / cast/streaming/impl/environment.cc
  core/cast/streaming/EncodedFrame.kt
      <- cast/streaming/public/frame_id.h / encoded_frame.h
  core/CastConstants.kt (the openscreen-derived constants, and the receiver
      application ids)
      <- cast/streaming/public/constants.h
         cast/common/public/cast_streaming_app_ids.h

Additional files in `core/` incorporate individual constants, message field
definitions, or wire-format facts described in openscreen headers; those files
cite the relevant openscreen path in their header comments.

